# Magr architecture

Keep this repo's Magr structure. Do not migrate to go_router, Riverpod, or a new `app/` folder.

## Layers

```
lib/features/<feature>/
  data/          models (Freezed JSON) + data sources + repository impl
  domain/        entities + repository contract + Requester
  presentation/  pages + widgets + cubits + AutoRoute pages
lib/core/        theme, widgets, http, bloc, routes, helpers — shared only
```

A widget used by **two features** moves to `core/widgets/`. A widget used by one feature stays in that feature's `presentation/widgets/` or `pages/<page>/widgets/`.

## Page files (mandatory Magr pattern)

```
pages/login/
  login_imports.dart      # imports + `part` directives
  login.dart              # part of imports; `@RoutePage()` widget
  login_controller.dart   # part of imports; no BuildContext stored
  widgets/
    login_widgets_imports.dart
    build_login_form.dart # `part of` widgets imports
```

- Screen is `StatefulWidget` only to own the controller. UI widgets are `StatelessWidget`.
- Controller holds `ObsValue`, `TextEditingController`, `GlobalKey`, `Requester` — not `setState`.
- Do not store `BuildContext` on the controller. Pass it into methods.

## Data mapping

API model (`*Model` + `toDomainModel()`) → domain entity. UI never reads JSON maps.

## Fake data first

Until the user asks for networking, screens use a fake repository returning static domain models. Keep `Requester` / repository contracts.
